<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5944" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">căchinnābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		cachinno (Appuleian). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Capable of laughing</i>, <i>laughing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo animal cachinnabile,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 33, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>pertaining to immoderate
				laughter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">risus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 132, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
